ncient Egyptian priesthood still around in the modern World of Darkness (and Isis is both a goddess of healing and magic) so they were my designated group to control access to the Spell of Life. And as a further access control, it could only be successfully cast in one of their temples within the Web of Faith.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All well and good, but, upon further reflection, I had another problem. There weren\u2019t really any gods hanging around anymore to actually facilitate this. The closest thing the modern World of Darkness has to all-powerful gods would probably be the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Celestine_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Celestines</a>, but they\u2019re\u2026not really what I needed here. I needed some old gods (or at least <b><i>one</i></b> old god) who was still hanging about. That got me thinking, while Exalted isn\u2019t canonically the long-lost past of the World of Darkness universe (though it was <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/li0rfo/found_an_old_exalted_ad_from_before_the_game_was/\" target=\"_blank\">originally going to be</a>), many fans still run with that, including me. Doing some digging, I found a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cytherea\" target=\"_blank\">Primordial</a> who could conceivably fit the bill, with just a bit of backstory fudging.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And this actually ended up being a better concept than I intended. Immortal champions created by a goddess to be her agents on Earth? Sounds a lot like the Exalted themselves, so I ran with the idea. The mummies being \u201cExalted Lite\u201d not only solved all my access control issues, it was another link to the Exalted setting, which I\u2019m all in favor of.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Though there were some unavoidable repercussions. One, the Bane Mummies couldn\u2019t exist as my new background story for the mummies would completely preclude that. Still, the Asekh-sen are pretty nasty already and the servants of Set can create those whenever they feel like, so they\u2019ll do as stand-ins for the Bane Mummies. Two, it would also preclude the Cabiri, but I liked having them around as another occasionally-seen-in-the-shadows faction, so I found a way to include them. Having just recently got around to picking up World of Darkness: Immortals, the Purified struck me as the perfect replacement for the Cabiri. These immortals were clearly meant as a homage to the Mummy sourcebooks, but they were inferior immortals when compared to the true mummies. But, since the Cabiri were said to be the creations of \u201ca bastardized variant of the Spell of Life,\u201d that actually worked out even more perfectly. I just needed to make the casting requirements to become one of these lesser immortals difficult as well in order to justify their rarity, and there you go.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">For the true mummies, however, I wanted to stress what I believe they ought to be doing, namely combatting the darkness in the World of Darkness. This appears to be what the 3<sup>rd</sup> Edition authors were (clumsily) attempting to do via the Judges of Ma\u2019at, but I wanted a less Big Brother approach to steering mummies towards the straight and narrow. Hence, the package of Merits that ensure they can\u2019t miss the monsters lurking in the shadows, and that they can\u2019t try to make friends with those monsters. No nagging parents looking over their shoulder, but their new nature is just fundamentally incompatible with evil, so this should eventually clue them in to what side they\u2019re on.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Anyhow, hopefully this answers your questions, but I\u2019m happy to clarify any points.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">P.S. If you want to explore further links between Exalted and the World of Darkness, I recommend <a href=\"https://holdenshearer.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> not-exactly-official supplement to the World of Darkness by one of the former Exalted developers.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I've read Exalted vs WoD, or at least some of it, there was an actual play somewhere and I believe one of the Solar ended up sacrificing themselves to kill an antideluvian.<br /> <br /> I'm more interested in the CofD Purified, and possible an Exalted/CofD crossover setting... But that's not what this thread is about.<br /> <br /> So I will just say that I've gone the other way with my custom splatt, in that, the problem of Immortality being more common - ie if the Purified ritual is available to anyone, then what is stopping them from being as common as Kindred... I'm happy to modify my setting to allow them be (and deal with what I consider the interesting consequences).<br /> <br /> Next KotE (without the K and the otE).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}